[
  {
    "id": "a1c0de0000000001",
    "type": "comment",
    "name": "Basic control — set your AC's IP in the \"Gree AC\" config node first",
    "info": "Core nodes only, no dashboard needed.\n\n1. Double-click the **Gree HVAC** node, edit the **Gree AC** config node and set **Host** to your AC's IP (use **Scan network** below to find it), or turn on *Resolve by MAC*. Multi-split systems: point it at the outdoor unit and enter the indoor unit's MAC (from the *Indoor units* button).\n2. Deploy, then click the inject buttons.\n\nInput: either `msg.payload` as a property object (`{\"power\":\"on\",\"mode\":\"cool\",\"temperature\":24}`) or `msg.topic` = property name with `msg.payload` = value. Unknown properties, read-only ones and invalid values are dropped with a warning. `msg.action` makes a request instead (`getProperties`, `getDeviceInfo`, `getSubUnits`, `getVendorProperties`, `setVendorProperties`, `getClock`, `setClock`, `setName`).\n\nOutputs: 1 = changes (`updated` from the device, `acknowledged` after a write), 2 = full property snapshot, 3 = diagnostics (`state`, `error`, `heartbeat`, `device_info`, …), 4 = responses to `msg.action`. See docs/PROTOCOL.md for every property and value.",
    "x": 320,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
